| !Run for !OpenTTD - RISC OS port of OpenTTD 14.1
| Built with GCCSDK GCC 10.2 (arm-riscos-gnueabihf), statically linked and
| converted to Absolute (AIF) files, so !SharedLibs isn't needed.

Set OpenTTD$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <OpenTTD$Dir>.!Sprites
| SDL finds the icon bar sprite (!OpenTTD) and name from the application
| directory. Older versions set this variable; clear it so it doesn't
| affect other SDL programs.
Unset SDL$IconSprite

| --- Runtime support -------------------------------------------------
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error OpenTTD needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error OpenTTD needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
| PThreadTicker (from UnixLib 5.0.1) holds the code that switches the
| game's threads, so it never runs from the game's own memory while
| another task is paged in. A copy in !System is used if it's there.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <OpenTTD$Dir>.PThrTicker

| --- Sound ------------------------------------------------------------
| Sound goes through SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager (freeware by
| John Duffell, not included), which mix with other programs' sound.
| To get them, download ssb.zip and merge its !System into yours:
|   https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html
| If they aren't there, DigitalRenderer is used instead, and with
| neither the game runs silently.
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.51 IfThere System:Modules.DRenderer Then RMLoad System:Modules.DRenderer
Set OpenTTD$Sound -s sdl
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.51 Set OpenTTD$Sound -s null

| --- Music ------------------------------------------------------------
| MIDI music is played through a General MIDI SoundFont: the one set up
| by !MIDISynth (MIDISynth$SoundFont), or a file called SoundFont in
| here. Without either (or without sound) the game has no music.
Set OpenTTD$Music -m null
IfThere <OpenTTD$Dir>.SoundFont Then Set OpenTTD$Music -m midisynth
If "<MIDISynth$SoundFont>"<>"" Then IfThere <MIDISynth$SoundFont> Then Set OpenTTD$Music -m midisynth
If "<OpenTTD$Sound>"="-s null" Then Set OpenTTD$Music -m null

| --- Online content ---------------------------------------------------
| Downloads from the online content service go over HTTPS through
| AcornSSL (part of RISC OS 5). Without it the game uses its own,
| slower download route.
RMEnsure AcornSSL 0.00 IfThere System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL Then RMLoad System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL

| --- Memory ---------------------------------------------------------
| The C heap lives in a dynamic area called "OpenTTD Heap" (up to 512MB),
| which is removed when the game quits.
WimpSlot -min 32768K -max 32768K
| --- Display ---------------------------------------------------------
| OpenTTD$Display: "fullscreen" (switches to a screen mode of that size)
|                  or "windowed" (a desktop window of that size).
| OpenTTD$Size:    width x height, e.g. 1280x720. Smaller runs faster.
Unset OpenTTD$Display
Unset OpenTTD$Size
| Default: a 1024x768 desktop window. Put a | in front of these two lines
| to use the choices from Game Options > Graphics instead.
Set OpenTTD$Display windowed
Set OpenTTD$Size 1024x768
| In a high resolution desktop mode (EX0 EY0, "180dpi") the window is
| drawn at double size so it looks the same as in a 90dpi mode. To turn
| that off, or to force a scale, remove the | from this line (1 = off,
| 2 to 4 = scale).
Unset SDL$WindowScale
| Set SDL$WindowScale 1
Set OpenTTD$Video sdl
If "<OpenTTD$Display>"<>"" Then Do Set OpenTTD$Video sdl:<OpenTTD$Display>
Unset OpenTTD$Res
If "<OpenTTD$Size>"<>"" Then Do Set OpenTTD$Res -r <OpenTTD$Size>

| --- Program -------------------------------------------------------
| openttd-fast is built for the NEON instructions of the Raspberry Pi 2
| and later (and other Cortex-A machines) and is used when it's there.
| To use the standard build instead, put a | in front of the IfThere line.
Set OpenTTD$Binary openttd
IfThere <OpenTTD$Dir>.openttd-fast Then Set OpenTTD$Binary openttd-fast

| --- Sprite drawing (the "blitter") ----------------------------------
| 32bpp-optimized  the default: quick, no water or light animation.
| 32bpp-anim       animated water and lights (slower).
| 32bpp-neon       draws sprites with NEON instructions (openttd-fast
|                  only). Experimental: try it and compare the Frame
|                  rate window. It uses more memory for sprites.
| To choose one, change the Set line below.
Set OpenTTD$Blitter 32bpp-optimized
| The standard build has no NEON blitter; fall back to the default.
If "<OpenTTD$Binary><OpenTTD$Blitter>"="openttd32bpp-neon" Then Set OpenTTD$Blitter 32bpp-optimized

| --- Diagnostics ---------------------------------------------------
| To log a memory report every 10 seconds (and the video driver's
| messages) to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.OpenTTDlog, remove the | from this line.
Unset OpenTTD$Debug
| Set OpenTTD$Debug -d driver=1

| "Do" expands the <variables> before the command runs (Run does not).
Do Run <OpenTTD$Dir>.<OpenTTD$Binary> -v <OpenTTD$Video> <OpenTTD$Res> -b <OpenTTD$Blitter> <OpenTTD$Music> <OpenTTD$Sound> <OpenTTD$Debug> %*0 2><Wimp$ScrapDir>.OpenTTDlog
